and $b^* := \frac{2 C_2}{\epsilon - C_3}$ minimizing $\underline{N}$
satisfy that $b_* \leq b^*$.
Let $\alpha$ be small enough and we consider that $\theta_{K+1}$ approximates $\theta^*$. 
Then, we have that
\begin{align*}
b_* \approx b^* \text{ and } \overline{K}(b_*)b_* \approx \underline{K}(b^*)b^*,
